Use asyncio.run() instead of the deprecated get_event_loop() pattern.

Python 3.14 removed the implicit creation of an event loop in
asyncio.get_event_loop(), so the launcher crashes on startup with:

  RuntimeError: There is no current event loop in thread 'MainThread'.

asyncio.run() is the supported replacement and creates/manages its own loop.

--- a/matrix-reminder-bot
+++ b/matrix-reminder-bot
@@ -5,6 +5,6 @@ try:
     from matrix_reminder_bot import main
 
     # Run the main function of the bot
-    asyncio.get_event_loop().run_until_complete(main.main())
+    asyncio.run(main.main())
 except ImportError as e:
     print("Unable to import matrix_reminder_bot.main:", e)
